cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AnvilNext 2.0 engine notes: reverse-engineering documentation from a VR conversion"
message: "If you use these notes, please cite them."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Firejumper93"
    alias: Firejumper93
    website: "https://github.com/Firejumper93"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Firejumper93/GhostReconWildlands-AnvilNext2.0-Documentation"
abstract: >-
  Structural documentation of Ubisoft's AnvilNext 2.0 engine as shipped in Tom
  Clancy's Ghost Recon Wildlands, produced by interoperability analysis during a
  native OpenXR VR conversion. Covers the binary layout, data formats, skeletons
  and rigs, the pose pipeline, cameras, weapons and attachments, rendering, the
  CRC32 reflection system, method, and verified negatives. Contains no game code
  or game data. Corrections and retractions are kept in the text rather than
  edited out, because the wrong readings were reasonable and reproducible.
keywords:
  - AnvilNext
  - Anvil
  - Ubisoft
  - reverse engineering
  - game engine
  - VR
  - OpenXR
  - Ghost Recon Wildlands
  - first person
  - first-person
  - first person view
  - FPV
  - head camera
  - head bone camera
  - camera mod
  - HumanIK
  - inverse kinematics
